   "id": 233291,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/b39ff77daea6890d.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Mizoguchi B, Valenzuela N./PeerJ)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>A research study showed a gene was alternatively spliced in two ways during embryonic development of the turtle based on environmental temperature. The image shows the two transcript variants.</p>\n<p>What kind of alternative splicing is in this example?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 723310,
     "content_html": "Exon skipping."
    },
    {
     "id": 723309,
     "content_html": "Mutually exclusive exons."
    },
    {
     "id": 723308,
     "content_html": "Alternative donor sites."
    },
    {
     "id": 723307,
     "content_html": "Intron retention."
    }
   ],
